OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCFreely issues and 5 Live medium
OL,4,Cwave switch-off
OL,5,
OL,6,FAnother week...another set of problems
OL,7,Ffor Freely.
OL,9,FThere have been claims online that some
OL,10,Fchannels were unavailable for an
OL,11,Fextended period of time.
OL,13,FIf this was indeed the case ` and not
OL,14,Fdown to problems with an individual set
OL,15,Ftop box or internet connection ` then
OL,16,Fit hardly builds confidence in the
OL,17,Fplatform.
OL,19,FWhere is the resilience? Especially in
OL,20,Fany national emergency.
OL,23,EPub: 23-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1787487087
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G2/6
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCFreely issues and 5 Live medium
OL,4,Cwave switch-off
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhere is the simplicity and ease of
OL,7,Fuse? Especially for those viewers who
OL,8,Fmay have disabilities or other
OL,9,Fvulnerabilities.
OL,11,FAs I have said before, turning off
OL,12,FFreeview and shifting to internet
OL,13,Fdelivery is only a realistic
OL,14,Fproposition once a large proportion of
OL,15,Fconsumers have done this for
OL,16,Fthemselves.
OL,18,FAt present there is no obvious major
OL,19,Fselling point and some clear
OL,20,Fdisadvantages.
OL,23,EPub: 23-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14103
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1787487087
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G3/6
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCFreely issues and 5 Live medium
OL,4,Cwave switch-off
OL,5,
OL,6,FNone of this means the debate needs to
OL,7,Fsimply be a choice between keeping all
OL,8,FDTT transmitters open or a complete
OL,9,Fshutdown.
OL,11,FA proper audit of smaller relay
OL,12,Ftransmitters might suggest that some of
OL,13,Fthem are no longer necessary or viable.
OL,14,FSome were built to improve analogue
OL,15,Fcoverage ` not to extend it.
OL,17,FI suspect the likely closure of 5 Live
OL,18,Fon medium wave could provide an
OL,19,Finteresting case study.
OL,23,EPub: 23-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14104
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1787487087
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G4/6
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCFreely issues and 5 Live medium
OL,4,Cwave switch-off
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe BBC appears to be closing 5 Live on
OL,7,Fmedium wave by stealth, shutting small
OL,8,Ftransmitters in reception blackspots.
OL,10,FIn most cases, listeners will need to
OL,11,Fchose between switching to DAB,
OL,12,Flistening through the TV or online
OL,13,Foptions including Smart Speakers.
OL,15,F5 Live, of course, is not on FM so
OL,16,Fthere is the risk a switch off could
OL,17,Flose the network listeners.
OL,19,FMy advice to the BBC would be to
OL,20,Fannounce a switch off date now ` let's
OL,21,Fsay 31st March 2027.
OL,23,EPub: 23-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14105
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1787487087
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G5/6
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCFreely issues and 5 Live medium
OL,4,Cwave switch-off
OL,5,
OL,6,FThen marketing should swing into
OL,7,Faction. Do everything possible to push
OL,8,Fpeople to the other options and
OL,9,Fhighlight the two really easy ones for
OL,10,Ftechnophobes ` listening via the TV or
OL,11,Fthe cheap DAB radios that are now
OL,12,Feasily available.
OL,14,FThere are now plenty of small,
OL,15,Finexpensive DAB radios which can be
OL,16,Fpowered by ordinary batteries. You can
OL,17,Fcarry them into the bathroom or out
OL,18,Finto the garden. They are not like the
OL,19,Fbulky, mains operated DAB radios on
OL,20,Fsale 20 years ago.
OL,23,EPub: 23-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,142,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14106
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F141A1787487087
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G6/6
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GOPINIONCFreely issues and 5 Live medium
OL,4,Cwave switch-off
OL,5,
OL,6,FThere is a precedent. When Radio 2 came
OL,7,Foff medium wave in 1990, there were
OL,8,Fstill plenty of radios in use which
OL,9,Fdidn't have FM. As I recall, a campaign
OL,10,Fto get listeners to switch to FM began
OL,11,Fabout 9 months earlier when Radio 2
OL,12,Ffinally stopped sharing its FM
OL,13,Ffrequency with Radio 1.
OL,15,FIf switching off AM still costs 5 Live
OL,16,Flisteners, then this should worry those
OL,17,Fcontemplating turning off Freeview.
OL,23,EPub: 23-Aug-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
